{
 "lines": [
  {
   "id": "VO-01",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 9.173,
   "text": "Three college friends put the same thousand dollars into the S and P five hundred, on the same day, and twenty years later, one had over ten times as much."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-02",
   "start": 9.321,
   "end": 11.576,
   "text": "Wait, how? It's the same money!"
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-03",
   "start": 11.725,
   "end": 16.959,
   "text": "That's tiny pieces of five hundred big companies, all bought at the start of two thousand six."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-04",
   "start": 17.058,
   "end": 22.992,
   "text": "Then came the two thousand eight crash, and by year-end, each thousand was worth about seven hundred seventy."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-05",
   "start": 23.091,
   "end": 26.512,
   "text": "Jay sells at year-end and hides the cash in a shoebox."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-06",
   "start": 26.611,
   "end": 32.415,
   "text": "Maya sells too, but buys back at the end of two thousand nine, after missing a twenty-six percent rebound."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-07",
   "start": 32.514,
   "end": 34.069,
   "text": "Sam does nothing at all."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-08",
   "start": 34.466,
   "end": 38.378,
   "text": "At first, Jay feels smart, because shoebox money can't crash."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-09",
   "start": 38.716,
   "end": 46.464,
   "text": "By the end of twenty twenty-five, Jay has seven hundred seventy, Maya about sixty-four hundred, and Sam about eight thousand."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-10",
   "start": 46.563,
   "end": 50.113,
   "text": "Same money, same day, and the friend who did nothing won."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-11",
   "start": 50.45,
   "end": 54.311,
   "text": "So if your money crashed, would you sell, wait or hold?"
  }
 ],
